        <mxCell id="n17" value="The two parsers matter because they end in the same call: one store, one way in, whether a vehicle&#10;was seen by ego's own camera or reported over the radio link. That identity is the phase's first&#10;acceptance box, and it is why the malformed-input corpus is tested against both parsers at once." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#f2f4f9;strokeColor=#e3e5ea;fontColor=#3d3d46;fontSize=15.4;align=left;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="502" width="800" height="74.69999999999999" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
